                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There's a real inventory bug reported at release where the game shows items in your possession, but the settlement dock interface reads it as empty — making the core resource-gathering loop feel broken, since there's no way to actually use what you scavenged. On top of that, enemies with heavier weapons can spot and land pinpoint hits on you from beyond your own visible zoom range, with no way to zoom out further to see them coming, which makes early encounters feel unfair rather than tactically challenging. Combined with a save system that isn't clearly signposted to new players, the difficulty ends up feeling more like a lack of information than a fair challenge. Fixing the inventory sync bug, giving players more visual range (or matching enemy detection range to what the player can actually see), and clarifying the save mechanic up front would make the punishing difficulty feel earned rather than arbitrary.",
